udent success. Be Part of Something Growing. Join a nursing department with a 50-year history of excellence, an ACEN-accredited Associate's and RN to BS in Nursing program, and a rapidly growing Practical Nursing Certificate Program. Help Build What Comes Next. This position offers the opportunity to contribute to curriculum development, student recruitment and retention, program assessment, clinical partnerships, and the continued growth of our Practical Nursing program. What You'll Do As a Practical Nursing Professor, you will: Create engaging and meaningful learning experiences in the classroom, skills lab, simulation, and clinical settings. Teach and evaluate students while helping them develop safe, competent, and compassionate nursing practices. Mentor and advise students throughout their nursing education. Contribute to curriculum development, program assessment, and continuous improvement. Support student recruitment, retention, and success. Help maintain strong relationships with clinical partners. Participate in faculty recruitment and evaluation, as well as other departmental responsibilities. Incorporate current evidence-based nursing practices and applicable state and program standards into instruction. Requirements: What We're Looking For- Required Qualifications: Master's degree in Nursing or Nursing Education; candidates with a bachelor's degree in nursing who are enrolled in and actively pursuing a master's degree or higher in nursing will also be considered. Current New York State Professional Nursing License. Current CPR certification. Strong teaching, clinical, communication, and computer skills. Excellent critical-thinking, problem-solving, and organizational abilities. Preferred Qualifications Doctorate in Nursing or a related field. Experience with simulation-based learning. Ready to Make a Difference? This is more than a faculty position?it's an opportunity to help shape the nurses of tomorrow. At Alfred State, you'll have the opportunity to bring your clinical experience and passion for nursing into a collaborative academic environment, work with innovative simulation technology, and play a meaningful role in the growth of a program preparing students for rewarding careers in healthcare. If you're ready to inspire, teach, mentor, and help build the future of nursing, we'd love to hear from you! Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. If you currently need sponsorship or will need it in the future to maintain employment authorization, you do not meet eligibility requirements. Additionally, please note that Alfred State College is not an E-Verify employer. Additional Information: The salary for this position is $80,000 . Employees are also offered EXCEPTIONAL BENEFITS!   We offer extensive healthcare and retirement options, including the opportunity for a pension. Furthermore, we prioritize a harmonious integration of work, personal life, and academic endeavors to support your overall work-life balance and effectiveness. Benefits options include: Health Insurance: Cost effective health insurance premiums with 73% to 88% covered by the employer. PPO or HMO option for personalized healthcare solutions. Exceptional fertility benefits available. Accumulated sick leave can cover a health insurance premium in retirement. Dental and Vision: No cost dental and vision benefits for employees and eligible dependents. Educational Support: Tuition benefits to invest in your continuous learning and professional development. Paid Time Off: New employees are eligible for up to an impressive 22 vacation and 13 paid sick days per year, increasing with years of service. Up to 13 paid holidays annually Paid parental leave Retirement Plans: Various retirement options, including a defined benefits (pension) plan.  With the pension, retired employees receive a defined monthly income for the rest of their life. Additional pre- and post- tax voluntary retirement savings options are available. Our comprehensive compe