    "https://alfredstate.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205449": {
      "title": "Executive Director of Admissions",
      "description": "Alfred State College\nJob Posting: Executive Director of Admissions Alfred State College \n\tJob Posting: Executive Director of Admissions Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Executive Director of Admissions Category: Management - MC Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Admissions Locations: Alfred, NY Posted: Oct 2, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time In-Person Position ID: 205449 Share About Alfred State College: Join a Mission That Matters at Alfred State College Are you ready to join our winning team? At top-ranked and growing Alfred State College, we transform lives by equipping students with the skills they need to succeed, providing upward mobility, and making higher education accessible to all. Known for affordability, exceptional academic support, and career-ready graduates, Alfred State is a place where your work truly makes a difference . Under the visionary leadership of President Steven Mauro, who joined the Pioneer family in 2022, Alfred State is committed to excellence through our dynamic Strategic Plan that cultivates our caring community, strengthens academic excellence, and attracts new Pioneers like you. With growing enrollment and a proven 98% employment and continuing education rate for graduates, this is your opportunity to join a thriving and forward-thinking institution while advancing your career. Teaching excellence is at the heart of Alfred State, creating a uniquely rewarding experience for educators to focus on student success. As a SUNY College of Technology, we offer a wide range of associate and bachelor's degrees building skills that are in demand with employers. Our focus on project-based learning and community engagement empowers students to develop real-world experience while offering a collaborative environment for our exceptional faculty and staff and is supported by extensive resources including more than 200 hands-on labs. At Alfred State College, we elevate graduates into respected Pioneer PROS . Our team supports students in launching rewarding careers while fulfilling our own personal and professional goals. We provide: Competitive compensation and comprehensive healthcare benefits. Opportunities for career advancement and professional development. A welcoming, collaborative campus community dedicated to innovation and student success. Live and Work in the Heart of the Ultimate College Town Nestled in Alfred, NY, our campus is part of the Western New York Wilds , a region known for its breathtaking natural beauty , outdoor adventure opportunities, and tight-knit community spirit. With nearby lakes, wetlands, farms, and state parks, Alfred offers peaceful surroundings and a chance to connect with nature.  Alfred isn't just a college town-it's been named the Ultimate College Town by Washington Post reporter Andrew Van Dam, who described Alfred as \"the collegiest\" in the nation since students comprise such a large portion of the community. Van Dam notes, \"If you go left at the town's only stoplight, you're on one campus. Turn right, you're on the other. Now that's a college town.\" In addition to a lively, academic atmosphere, Alfred offers: Creative and cultural experiences: Galleries, studios, artists, makers, performances, and artistic expression abound. Affordable living: A lower cost of living compared to larger cities makes Alfred an ideal place to call home and know your neighbors. A welcoming community: Friendly locals and a strong sense of belonging resonate as the entire community is focused on education. Exceptional K-12 schools: Nearby Alfred-Almond High School consistently earns top rankings in the state and region. Picture Yourself Here Located in a picturesque valley in New York's Southern Tier, Alfred is just 1-2 hours from the vibrant metropolitan areas of Rochester and Buffalo, as well as the Finger Lakes region, known for its festivals, scenic landscapes, and cultural attractions. Whether you're looking for a fulfilling career, a supportive community, or the perfect blend of professional opportunity and natural beauty, Alfred State College is more than a workplace, it's a place to thrive. Start your journey with us and discover the difference you can make at Alfred State College. Job Description: Alfred State College seeks a dynamic, relationship-centered, and forward-thinking Executive Director of Admissions to provide strategic leadership for undergraduate admissions and recruitment. Reporting to the Vice President for Enrollment Management, the Executive Director will lead a talented admissions team responsible for attracting, recruiting, admitting, and enrolling students who will thrive at Alfred State. The successful candidate will build upon recent enrollment momentum while helping the College evolve its recruitment strategy for a changing higher education marketplace. The Executive Director will preserve and strengthen Alfred State's longstanding relationships with high school counselors and other educational partners while expanding the College's reach in priority markets. Particular attention will be given to sustaining strong traditional undergraduate recruitment in New York State while increasing enrollment among out-of-state students, transfer students, online learners, and adult and professional learners. The ideal candidate will be a relationship-driven, data-informed leader who combines strategic thinking with strong operational execution, embraces technology and innovation, develops people, and works collaboratively across the institution to achieve enrollment goals. Why This Is a Distinctive Leadership Opportunity Strong Institutional and Enrollment Momentum - Alfred State enters Fall 2026 with its largest overall enrollment in more than 40 years and several years of positive recruitment performance. The College is also in a strong financial position and is completing a comprehensive capital campaign that is on pace to significantly exceed its ambitious $40 million goal. A College Preparing for Its Next Strategic Chapter - Alfred State is completing a successful five-year strategic plan in which its established goals have been achieved. Development of the next institutional strategic plan is underway, creating an opportunity for the Executive Director to help shape how enrollment strategy supports the College's next priorities. An Established Team and Integrated Enrollment Division - The Executive Director will lead a fully staffed admissions organization that includes experienced recruitment and enrollment operations professionals. Admissions operates within an integrated Enrollment Management division with close collaboration among Student Records and Financial Services, Marketing and Communications, and adult and career education enrollment. Modern Recruitment Technology and Innovation - Alfred State has invested significantly in recruitment technology and operates within an optimized Slate CRM environment that supports communication automation, segmentation, application management, reporting, and enrollment strategy. The College has also incorporated artificial intelligence and automation, including AI-assisted transcript reading and processing and front-desk engagement tools. Accessible Data and Strong Executive Partnership - Admissions leadership has access to enrollment funnel data, historical trends, program-level reporting, recruitment analytics, and Institutional Research dashboards. The Executive Director will serve as a strategic partner to the Vice President for Enrollment Management in enrollment planning, market analysis, recruitment investment, financial aid strategy, and long-range enrollment planning. An Opportunity to Build on Success - With traditional undergraduate recruitment performing well, the next Executive Director will have the opportunity to sharpen Alfred State's approach to out-of-state recruitment, transfer enrollment, online programs, adult learners, workforce development, territory optimization, and emerging markets while continuing to strengthen relationships with high school counselors and educational partners throughout New York State and beyond. Leadership Portfolio Enrollment Strategy, Analytics, and Market Development Provide leadership and direction for undergraduate admissions and recruitment in alignment with institutional enrollment goals. Partner with the Vice President for Enrollment Management to develop annual and multi-year recruitment strategies based on enrollment trends, market conditions, demographic changes, institutional priorities, and academic program opportunities. Use application, admission, deposit, yield, melt, visit, territory, event, and enrollment data to evaluate performance, identify opportunities, and adjust strategy throughout the recruitment cycle. Lead traditional first-year recruitment while strengthening strategies for out-of-state students, transfer students, online learners, adult and professional learners, and other priority populations. Develop and regularly evaluate recruitment territories using enrollment outcomes, market potential, staff capacity, travel costs, and return on investment. Collaborate with academic leadership to identify programs with enrollment growth potential and develop targeted recruitment strategies. Maintain a working knowledge of financial aid, scholarships, affordability, and financial aid leveraging strategies and their impact on recruitment and yield. Relationship Development and Recruitment Preserve, strengthen, and expand Alfred State's relationships with high school counselors throughout New York State and beyond. Build productive relationships with community college partners, school districts, BOCES, industry partners, community organizations, students, and families. Ensure the Admissions Office maintains a visible, responsive, and student-centered presence in the communities and markets it serves. Staff Leadership and Development Recruit, supervise, mentor, and develop admissions professionals while fostering a goal-oriented, data-informed culture of accountability, collaboration, professional growth, and student-centered service. Coach admissions counselors in effective student and family engagement, including relationship building, questioning and discovery techniques, telephone and virtual communication, follow-up strategy, program positioning, addressing concerns, and communicating the value of an Alfred State education. Establish consistent recruitment best practices and develop staff understanding of territory performance, conversion patterns, enrollment metrics, and institutional goals. Support staff development through coaching, professional development, meaningful delegation, and opportunities for increased responsibility. Technology, Communications, and Enrollment Operations Champion sophisticated use of Slate CRM as a recruitment, communication, marketing automation, territory management, and enrollment intelligence platform. Partner with Enrollment Management, Marketing and Communications, and technology staff to improve data architecture, communication plans, segmentation, automation, personalization, and prospective student engagement. Identify opportunities to use artificial intelligence, digital communication tools, workflow automation, and other emerging technologies to improve responsiveness, accuracy, productivity, and recruitment effectiveness. Provide executive oversight of admissions operations to ensure timely, accurate, consistent, and student-centered application review and processing. Ensure effective management of admission decisions, program capacity, waitlists, special populations, and related admissions processes. Events, Yield, and Campus Collaboration Provide strategic leadership for campus visits, Open Houses, admitted student programs, regional recruitment events, counselor programs, and other enrollment events. Use recruitment events intentionally as conversion and yield strategies, with clear objectives, outcome tracking, and continuous improvement. Build strong partnerships with Academic Affairs, Marketing and Communications, Student Records and Financial Services, Student Affairs, EOP, ASAP/ACE, Athletics, and other campus stakeholders. Participate actively in enrollment, onboarding, retention, and student success initiatives, recognizing recruitment and retention as connected parts of the student lifecycle. Requirements: Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree and 5+ years of progressive professional experience in college admissions, enrollment management, student recruitment, or a closely related field. Demonstrated supervisory or team leadership experience. Demonstrated ability to develop and execute recruitment strategies with a proven record of achieving enrollment goals, improving key recruitment metrics, or contributing to sustained enrollment growth. Experience using enrollment data and recruitment metrics to inform strategy and decision-making. Exceptional interpersonal and communication skills, with demonstrated success building relationships with students, families, school counselors, colleagues, and external partners. Experience working with CRM or enrollment technology systems. Ability to manage multiple priorities, lead through change, and make informed decisions in a fast-moving, results-oriented environment. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in higher education, enrollment management, business, marketing, communications, student affairs, or a related field. Significant leadership experience within a college or university admissions operation. Advanced experience with Slate CRM, including recruitment communications, automation, reporting, queries, territories, or related functionality. Experience developing and managing recruitment territories using enrollment performance, market analysis, and return-on-investment measures. Experience with out-of-state recruitment, transfer enrollment, online enrollment, adult learner recruitment, or other emerging enrollment populations. Experience developing or leading campus visit, recruitment, and yield programs. Working knowledge of financial aid, institutional scholarships, and enrollment leveraging strategies. Experience partnering with academic programs or faculty on program-specific enrollment strategies. Experience using digital engagement, marketing automation, artificial intelligence, or emerging technologies within recruitment and enrollment operations. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. If you currently need sponsorship or will need it in the future to maintain employment authorization, you do not meet eligibility requirements. Additionally, please note that Alfred State College is not an E-Verify employer. Additional Information: The salary for this position starts at $105,000 and is commensurate with education and experience. Employees are also offered EXCEPTIONAL BENEFITS!   We offer extensive healthcare and retirement options, including the opportunity for a pension. Furthermore, we prioritize a harmonious integration of work, personal life, and academic endeavors to support your overall work-life balance and effectiveness. Benefits options include: Health Insurance: Cost effective health insurance premiums with 73% to 88% covered by the employer. PPO or HMO option for personalized healthcare solutions. Exceptional fertility benefits available. Accumulated sick leave can cover a health insurance premium in retirement. Dental and Vision: No cost dental and vision benefits for employees and eligible dependents. Educational Support: Tuition benefits to invest in your continuous learning and professional development. Paid Time Off: New employees are eligible for up to an impressive 22 vacation and 13 paid sick days per year, increasing with years of service. Up to 13 paid holidays annually Paid parental leave Retirement Plans: Various retirement options, including a defined benefits (pension) plan.  With the pension, retired employees receive a defined monthly income for the rest of their life. Additional pre- and post- tax voluntary retirement savings options are available. Our comprehensive compensation and benefits package are designed to exceed your expectations, affirming our dedication to your overall well-being and professional growth. Non-Discrimination Notice Alfred State College hereby advises students, parents, employees, and the general public that it offers employment and educational opportunities, including career and technical educational opportunities, without regard to an individual's race/color, national origin, creed/religion, age, disability, sex, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, citizenship or immigration status, pregnancy-related condition, predisposing genetic characteristics, military status, victim of domestic violence, victim of retaliation, conviction record, arrest record, lawful source of income, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, New York State, or local law. Employees, students, applicants, or other members of the college community (including but not limited to vendors, visitors, and guests) may not be subjected to harassment that is prohibited by law or treated adversely or retaliated against based upon a protected characteristic. Alfred State policy is in accordance with federal and state laws and regulations prohibiting discrimination and harassment. These laws include the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Title VI of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964 as Amended by the Equal Employment Opportunity Act of 1972, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, and the New York State Human Rights Law. If you have questions about this notice or would like to file a grievance, please contact our Director of Institutional Compliance & Equity: Kayleigh Jones Director of Institutional Compliance & Equity Alfred State College 10 Upper College Drive Alfred, NY 14802 Email: cdo@alfredstate.edu Phone: 607-587-4026 If you would like to receive the combined Annual Security and Fire Safety Report which contains this information, you can stop in and request one at the University Police Department, located in the TG House on Lower College Drive or request a copy by calling the University Police at 607-587-3999. This report is available on the college's website at: http://www.alfredstate.edu/university-police/annual-security-and-fire-safety-report Application Instructions: Returning applicants may login to their Alfred State College Careers Account to apply for this position. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. The following documents MUST be submitted to be considered for this position: Resume/CV Cover Letter Alfred State College is committed to providing equal employment opportunities for individuals with disabilities. In support of this commitment, reasonable accommodations will be made to ensure that qualified applicants with disabilities or pregnancy-related conditions can participate fully in the application, interview, and selection process, and perform the essential functions of the position. Applicants are encouraged to request accommodations in a timely manner by contacting the Office of Human Resources at 607-587-4025 or emailing hr@alfredstate.edu . Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Alfred State College 10 Upper College Dr. Alfred, NY 14802"
